  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COVID-19 Pacific and Timor-Leste Preparedness and Recovery Non-government Organisation Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provides funding to non-government organisations (NGOs) to support communities in the Pacific and Timor-Leste to prepare for, respond to and recover from COVID-19. It provides multi-sectoral, flexible support, tailored to individual country contexts. It includes support to food security and livelihoods, health services and hygiene promotion, water and sanitation facilities, social protection measures and gender-based violence support services. It uses existing NGO funding mechanisms, focused on countries with the highest absorptive capacity and need (including Timor-Leste, PNG, Solomon Islands, Fiji and Vanuatu). It builds on already existing NGO support in target countries and includes specific activities focused on gender, disability inclusion and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
